
# Abstract concepts

concept
    nothing
    something
    someone

    # Weather components. rain/snow/fog/wind carry a strength-measurement;
    # sky carries a sky-condition.
    weather             (obs) (tar @excl)
        rain            (tar @excl strength-measurement)
        snow            (tar @excl strength-measurement)
        fog             (tar @excl strength-measurement)
        wind            (tar @excl strength-measurement)
        sky             (tar @excl sky-condition)
        thunder         (obs) (tar @excl strength-measurement)
        temperature     (obs) (tar @excl)

    phrase
        yes
        no

    # Sidedness. Used by sided actions (REACH_FOR, GRASP, ARM_DRINK, ...) to
    # designate which arm/hand engages. The (side ?x) rule-function evaluates
    # to one of these by reading /side off the symbol's kind.
    side
        left  (side left)
        right (side right)

    availability        (sub building)  (tar @excl)
        for-sale
        for-rent
        off-the-market

    # A general open/shut STATUS. The value kinds for perceivable open/closed
    # states - e.g. the struct-status attr on interior-space (common.arc): a room
    # reads `open` while its premises trade and `closed` once shuttered (perceived
    # on sight, so a worker who steps into a closed room learns his firm has folded).
    status
        open
        closed

    # An opening's leaf position (@excl - one at a time): ajar = a passable gap,
    # shut = the leaf drawn to (still openable if unlocked). The opening-status attr
    # on a door / window (structure-part.arc), perceived on sight. Unset reads neither.
    opening-status      (tar @excl)
        ajar
        shut

    # An opening's lock state (@excl). The lock-status attr on a door / window.
    # Default is unset = NOT locked (an openable door); a residence locks up via an
    # explicit set. Perceived on sight so a thief can case it.
    lock-status         (tar @excl)
        locked
        unlocked

    # Structural integrity of an opening (@excl - distinct from the life-state
    # `condition` axis). The integrity attr on a door / window: intact until forced
    # or smashed, then broken (a broken leaf is a permanent passable gap). Perceived.
    integrity           (tar @excl)
        intact
        broken

    # Discretion of an acquisition (@excl): covert = leave no trace to me (steal /
    # hire someone), overt = the ordinary open purchase. Rides the aux of an acquire
    # task; rules test only [k covert], anything else is overt by default.
    discretion          (tar @excl)
        covert
        overt

    legal-right
        property        (sub being)

    # Held-VALUE taxonomy: the virtues a person can be attested to hold via
    # {person value <kind>} attitude beliefs (States.mon `value`). The wrong-act
    # reflex gate compares an act's (contradicts <kind>) declaration against
    # them; `property` reuses the legal-right kind above.
    held-value
        life
        safety
        trust
        liberty
        kin-loyalty
        privacy

    # Life-state axis (@excl - one value at a time per subject). alive is the
    # universal default (the condition attr's default value); a dead-mint
    # supersedes it via @excl contradiction resolution at every channel (percept
    # mirror, told, read, begin-belief) with no explicit end. consumed is the
    # prop twin of dead - an eaten / drunk / used-up consumable - minted ongoing
    # and never ended, superseding the prop's default alive.
    condition           (tar @excl)
        alive
        dead
        consumed

    # Consciousness axis (@excl), HUMAN-NPC only - the awareness attr is listed
    # on human-npc alone, so props never carry it. Default conscious; a subdue
    # blow writes unconscious, recovery / re-observation writes conscious back.
    # The physical-mobility classifier reads the awareness attr for bedridden.
    awareness           (tar @excl)
        conscious
        unconscious

    # Interment axis (@excl), HUMAN-NPC only. Default unburied; the burial rite
    # mints buried (belief-only - the rite destroys the entity), which supersedes
    # the unburied percept in every witness. The bury / convey lanes cast off the
    # positive unburied belief; the standing dead + unburied pair is the body-state
    # that drives those duty lanes.
    internment          (tar @excl)
        unburied
        buried

    # The discrete de-quantization of the continuous `fatigue` attr, minted as a
    # {@self alertness <kind>} self-belief by the fatigue appraiser (the queryable
    # memory of tiredness; the physiology + sleep-pull utility read the attr).
    alertness           (tar @excl)
        alert
        tired
        sleepy

    # The discrete de-quantization of the continuous `hunger` attr, minted as
    # a {@self satiety <kind>} self-belief by the physiology appraiser (like
    # `alertness` over `fatigue`). The meal lanes gate eligibility on the
    # attr; consumers of the BELIEF are the body couplings (mood; physical
    # weakness arrives with the combat spec) and the famished starvation
    # tail.
    satiety             (tar @excl)
        sated
        hungry
        famished

    # Observable locomotion level - the physical-mobility state, mirrored
    # directly as a belief (like `condition` / `alertness`; no separate
    # relation). Derived in hsim_derive::classify_physical_mobility from
    # condition + awareness + age. Distinct from `alertness` (sleep / wake),
    # from `condition` (alive / dead) and from `awareness` (conscious /
    # unconscious): physical-mobility captures what an NPC can DO physically when
    # conscious. The bedridden value covers both genuine incapacity
    # (severe injury) and the social state of staying-in-bed;
    # physical-mobility being derived means the same symbol can mean both
    # as the substrate behind it varies.
    physical-mobility   (tar @excl)
        mobile
        crutch-assisted
        wheelchair-bound
        bedridden

    # Existential-frame taxonomy. The target of the `life-aim` drive in
    # States.mon: what an NPC wants their LIFE to amount to. Distinct
    # from `calling` (the specific DOMAIN one wants to excel in - music,
    # engineering, soldiering): same musician (calling=music) can hold
    # life-aim=wealth-aim (mercenary success), life-aim=legacy-aim (be
    # remembered), or life-aim=belonging-aim (just play in the local pub
    # band). Derived annually by hsim_derive::classify_life_aim from
    # substrate (Big Five + Dark Tetrad + class trajectory + bond counts
    # + worship). NOT @excl - the classifier explicitly end-dates the
    # prior dominant life-aim belief on a qualitative shift (PR-aim-
    # history), so multi-decade life-aim history is queryable as
    # repeated {@self life-aim ?} beliefs with non-overlapping intervals.
    life-aim            (tar)  (disclosure friend)
        legacy-aim
        wealth-aim
        piety-aim
        respectability-aim
        autonomy-aim
        power-aim
        belonging-aim

    # A predator's stable victim-type FIXATION (serial_predation Phase 2,
    # generalized): repeated {@self fixation <trait-value>} beliefs whose
    # conjunction is the victim-type PROFILE (e.g. {fixation tall} +
    # {fixation blonde} + {fixation male} = "tall blond men"). Each target
    # is any physical / social trait-value kind (a gender / height / girth /
    # appearance / hair-color / eye-color / nationality / class-situation /
    # job leaf); the value's parent kind IS its axis, so the matcher reads
    # the right attr / belief / job generically. NOT @excl - a profile is
    # several beliefs. Seeded once per predator by copying 1-2 traits off a
    # random "type prototype" person, so victim-type consistency EMERGES
    # (and the profile is guaranteed achievable). Renders in the rap-sheet.
    fixation            (sub human)  (tar ?)

    # (method / method_means RETIRED: choose_kill_method no longer mints a chosen-MO
    # belief - it PROPOSES the killing task directly from kill_method_table each cycle,
    # so the method is re-picked on the fly rather than latched into a belief.)

    # Unified domain axis (PR-skill-life). ONE hierarchical taxonomy that
    # `interest`, `skilled-in`, and `calling` (States.mon) all target as three
    # progressive bands on the same axis: casual pull -> earned competence ->
    # life mission. They COMPOSE (an NPC may hold all three on one domain).
    # Replaces the former separate `interest` / `skill_kind` / `field_of_study`
    # enums; their leaves are re-parented here unchanged (the `medicine`
    # duplicate that lived in both skill_kind and field_of_study is deduped to
    # one leaf). `t_ontology::is_a` answers "any martial skill?" / "any academic
    # field?" in one query. The semantic categories group the practicable
    # competences (academic-field / performance-art / martial / illicit /
    # athletics / pastime / social-craft) and the non-practicable topical
    # interests (avocation / devotional / civic) an NPC may hold an `interest`
    # in without ever being `skilled-in` it.
    #
    # A domain is ALSO what an act's (track-skill-level <domain>) decoration
    # names, so the pipeline accrues competence to it as the act is performed
    # (act_skill.h). That makes the DEPTH of this tree the granularity dial:
    # kind matching is subsumptive, so an act decorated with a leaf
    # (marksmanship) still answers a category-level read (martial). Decorate at
    # the level the competence is really earned at.
    domain
        # Studied disciplines (former field_of_study) + scholarly topics.
        academic-field
            classics
            engineering
            medicine
            law
            theology
            commerce
            natural-science
            accountancy
            navigation
            husbandry
            primary-school-curriculum
            secondary-school-curriculum
            history
            science
            # Reading and writing as ONE earned competence - the literate NPC
            # takes in a document and drafts a clear letter. Distinct from
            # `literature` (performance-art), which is the literary ART, and
            # from the `writing` attr, which is a document's text.
            literacy
        # Expressive / cultural arts.
        performance-art
            music
            theatre
            literature
        # Combat / physical skills (former skill_kind combat leaves).
        martial
            marksmanship
            knife-fighting
            swordsmanship
            pugilism
            wrestling
            horsemanship
            riding
        # Criminal competences (former skill_kind operational leaves).
        illicit
            poisoning-knowledge
            forgery
            lockpicking
            climbing
            evading
            detecting
            # garrotting: the footpad / street-violence craft (the 1862
            # garrotting panic) - the silent approach, the cosh, the
            # ligature. The recidivist's competence, distinct from a
            # one-off desperate labourer's brute strength. skill-affinity
            # maps it to strangle / bludgeon (perpetration.hs). Held by
            # ticket-of-leave men + career footpads in the for-hire pool.
            garrotting
        # Physical recreation (the `sports` interest). NOT the standalone
        # `sport` competition-discipline enum below (cricket / rowing / ...),
        # which is the achievement target of the win achievement belief.
        athletics
            sports
        # Practised leisure: recreational competences one measurably gets better
        # at, unlike the topical `avocation` interests below. `gaming` is skill
        # at the table - reading opponents, the odds, the bluff - across every
        # game kind; the money/non-money split is the (gambling) FACET on the
        # game, not a branch here.
        pastime
            gaming
        # The social crafts: competences at handling other PEOPLE, as opposed to
        # a subject (academic-field), a body (martial / athletics) or a tool.
        social-craft
            # Running and adjudicating a proceeding - a club meet, a race, a
            # service. The competence behind the duties an office carries.
            officiating
            # Drawing another into intimacy against the odds.
            seduction
            # Judging, hiring, promoting and dismissing staff - the duty lane an
            # org officer performs (org_duties, duty-tables.mc). The `work` task
            # itself is a SHELL (it proposes the held duty and DWELL), so the
            # competence lives on the specific duty tasks, never on `work`.
            personnel
        # Topical interests one holds without practising a skill.
        avocation
            antiques
        devotional
            religion
            spiritualism
        civic
            suffrage

    # Competence-level enum - the /aux of `skilled-in` beliefs. Novice
    # is the entry tier; trained takes years of practice; expert is the
    # cap reachable through profession tenure or apprenticeship-to-
    # master. Future tier (master) may land if a 4th band is needed for
    # exceptional NPCs.
    competence-level    (tar @excl)
        novice
        trained
        expert

    # skill-level - the /aux of {@self skill-level {act} <rung>} beliefs the action
    # pipeline emits as an act decorated (track-skill-level) is performed and its
    # per-act competence crosses a band (skill_level_pipeline_plan.md). The 4-rung
    # ladder that supersedes competence-level; leaf names avoid competence-level's
    # (novice/trained/expert) and vocational-state's (master) since kind leaves are
    # global, and both coexist until the skilled-in retirement (plan P4).
    skill-level         (tar @excl)
        beginner
        competent
        proficient
        virtuoso

    # school-grade - the /aux of {@self school-grades <school> <grade>} beliefs,
    # minted when an NPC graduates a school. The letter-grade credential earned at
    # a curriculum level; distinct from skill-level (act-earned competence). This is
    # what skilled-in [k <school>_curriculum] used to stand in for.
    school-grade        (tar @excl)
        A
        B
        C
        D
        F

    # Military rank - the /aux of a seeded `served` self-belief (States.mon):
    # {@self served <unit> /aux <rank>}. Scales the martial skill band a
    # veteran/serving soldier carries (a colonel out-shoots a private) and
    # the contract-killing fee. The officer tier (ensign+) is gentry-born -
    # the fallen-officer killer an upper-class instigator can reach directly
    # (the Sebastian Moran case). Seeded by seed_military_service.
    military-rank       (tar @excl)
        private
        corporal
        sergeant
        ensign
        lieutenant
        captain
        major
        colonel

    # (Relational stance no longer uses band-kind aux taxonomies; the continuous
    # warmth/esteem/trust/attraction scalar projects directly to infinitive
    # verb-state beliefs - like/dislike/admire/... - declared in States.mon's
    # (stance) block. See Docs/social/relational_stance.md.)

    death-cause         (tar @excl)
        disease
        accident
        old-age
        childbirth
        violence
        suicide
        # The covert kill: no violent mechanism in the body, so a burial
        # verdict (serial_predation Phase 1) reads the corpse as natural.
        # Written by the poison kill terminal; the divergence between this
        # body-truth and the village's circumstance-of-death story is the
        # detective's case. Named `poisoning` (the manner of death), not
        # `poison`: the bare term is already the kill TASK relation and a
        # noun-state would collide with it.
        poisoning

    # Specific diseases an NPC can have. Distinct
    # from `death-cause disease` which is the cause-of-death enum value;
    # this taxonomy names the specific pathology (consumption /
    # cholera / etc.). Future env attr `disease` (kind, /reason or
    # /imperceptible per knowledge_design_notes.md - reading it requires
    # a DIAGNOSE action by a competent physician, not passive
    # perception) will hold one of these values per sick NPC. Sub-kinds
    # are starter content for 1897 medical reality; extend as content
    # demands.
    disease
        consumption
        cholera
        smallpox
        typhus
        dysentery
        influenza
        scarlet-fever
        pneumonia

    # Observable symptoms. Distinct from disease:
    # symptoms are what others SEE (cough / fever / pallor / weakness);
    # the disease is the diagnosis a physician INFERS from symptoms. Each
    # leaf has a corresponding env attr on body archetypes (per obs);
    # the disease attr is /reason or /imperceptible. Starter set; extend
    # as content demands.
    symptom
        cough
        fever
        pallor
        weakness
        rash
        chills

    # Cause-of-death narrative witnesses form when
    # perceiving a death scene (vs death-cause, the objective cause). Used
    # in `circumstance-of-death` beliefs that F2 gossip carries
    # village-wide; the "staged story" emerges from observers agreeing on
    # a particular incident kind. Extensible as new staging shapes are
    # authored.
    incident
        burglary
        domestic-violence
        accident
        duel
        illness-complication

    # Region mood components (the mood-kinds attr is plural - a region carries
    # several at once, so no @excl).
    mood
        anti-aristocratic
        anti-outsider
        plague-fear
        pro-reform
        war-weariness

    # Personal emotion - transient affective states, held as the noun-state
    # {subject emotion <kind>}. /sub human, so {?other emotion anger} is a
    # valid held belief (theory of mind for free). Non-@excl: emotions
    # coexist (joy about one thing, grief about another). /tar is omitted, so
    # the target defaults to emotion's own subkinds. The directed "about"
    # focus rides in the belief's aux field. See Docs/emotion/emotion_system.md.
    emotion             (sub human)
        joy
        pride
        hope
        relief
        gratitude
        affection
        grief
        distress
        anger
        fear
        shame
        guilt
        envy
        jealousy
        disgust
        contempt
        # admiration: positive esteem - looking UP at competence / honour /
        # virtue (the sibling of contempt). Minted by honour-act; the Class I
        # stance coupling routes it to esteem+.
        admiration
        # longing: the felt pull of attraction - the transient affective surface
        # of the durable attraction scalar (fancy/desire/crave verb-states).
        # Minted by the standing attraction driver toward a mate-valued
        # target. Named `longing`, not `desire`, to
        # avoid colliding with the `desire` attraction verb-state label. No stance
        # coupling row: the attraction scalar is already driven by mate-value, so
        # this is a pure feeling (mood / NLG surface), not a stance re-driver.
        longing

    # Personal pressure - second-order standing motivational loads that build
    # when beliefs + drives + appraisals + constraints converge (plan section
    # 10.3-AFFECT item A). Parallel to emotion in shape - {subject pressure
    # <kind>} with the directed focus in aux - but with multi-week to
    # multi-year salience windows (vs emotion's hours to days) and a
    # different mood contribution (pressures feed the `stress` dimension, not
    # contentment / agitation). Non-@excl: pressures stack - the layered
    # motive a deliberation event reads IS the stacked pressure set.
    pressure            (sub human)
        status-loss
        attachment-loss
        autonomy-loss
        exposure-risk
        resource-scarcity
        humiliation
        injustice
        moral-violation
        existential-threat
        obligation-strain
        rivalry-pressure

    # Justifying narratives - the cognitive frames an NPC holds to make a
    # past or planned harmful act acceptable to themselves (plan section
    # 10.3-AFFECT item E). Target of the `justify` attitude
    # (States.mon): {@self justify they-deserved-it /aux <victim>}. The held
    # narrative discounts inhibition; a guilty NPC's justify beliefs are
    # queryable through interrogation in isim. Different perpetrators hold
    # different narratives; a non-guilty NPC holds none.
    narrative
        they-deserved-it
        i-had-no-choice
        it-was-necessary
        everyone-does-this
        i-was-protecting-kin
        they-are-subhuman
        the-law-is-unjust
        self-defense

    # Role-identities an NPC self-identifies as. Held as {@self identity
    # <role>} self-beliefs; derived by hsim_derive::classify_identities from
    # substrate state (kids -> parent, spouse -> spouse, job -> worker,
    # church member -> christian, class + gender -> gentleman / lady, job
    # kind -> merchant / servant / soldier / steward, Dark Tetrad attr ->
    # machiavellian / sadist, low assertiveness composite -> coward);
    # future PRs add explicit identity-adoption events. Read by the
    # deliberate synthesizer to anchor floor branches (more identities ->
    # more anchored -> more likely to forgive / do_nothing); by
    # categorize() to shift thresholds when an anchor's parties overlap
    # the appraiser's identity-relevant relations (a parent identity makes
    # child-related construals more salient); by the justify pick to bias
    # which narrative an actor reaches for (a parent reaches for
    # i-was-protecting-kin, a christian-priest for it-was-necessary); and
    # by perpetration.hsc method rows' :id-dampens / :id-boosts to bias
    # method selection (a gentleman dampens public_confront, a sadist
    # boosts cook_alive).
    # Non-@excl - an NPC's composite identity IS the held set.
    # Atom names are `<X>_role` to avoid colliding with existing kinds of
    # the same bare name (parent / spouse are relationship bonds;
    # merchant / steward are job kinds; etc.). The `_role` suffix reads
    # naturally when minted: `{@self identity parent-role}` = "I identify
    # as a parent."
    role
        parent-role
        spouse-role
        worker-role
        christian-role
        gentleman-role
        lady-role
        merchant-role
        servant-role
        soldier-role
        steward-role
        # Dark Tetrad and trait-composite identities.
        # machiavellian / sadist read the homonymous Dark Tetrad attr
        # against a tunable threshold in situations.hsc; coward fires on
        # EITHER (low assertiveness AND high withdrawal) OR (high
        # inhibition AND not-respectable).
        machiavellian-role
        sadist-role
        coward-role
        # Skill-driven trade / talent identities (PR-skill-life S8). Derived by
        # classify_identities from a held {@self skilled-in <domain>} at >=
        # trained: physician <- medicine, lawyer <- law, scholar <- any other
        # academic-field, soldier (soldier-role above) <- martial, musician <-
        # music, artist <- other performance-art (theatre / literature),
        # sportsman <- athletics. The competence (not the job title) confers the
        # identity, so a trained-in-medicine apothecary still identifies as a
        # physician. Composite (non-@excl): a polymath holds several.
        physician-role
        lawyer-role
        scholar-role
        musician-role
        artist-role
        sportsman-role

    # Interests are now `{@self interest <domain>}` beliefs (the casual-pull
    # band of the unified `domain` axis above); `interest` is an explicit
    # verb-state in States.mon. The former standalone `interest` topic enum was
    # folded into `domain` (PR-skill-life): music/theatre/literature ->
    # performance-art, history/science -> academic-field, riding -> martial,
    # sports -> athletics, religion/spiritualism -> devotional, antiques ->
    # avocation, suffrage -> civic. Still seeded as hereditary self-beliefs in
    # mx_make_human and grown / shed by interest_acquired / interest_lost.

    # Competitive sports - the target of the win achievement
    # belief (States.mon), written by the sporting_event hsim event. A `sport`
    # is the competition discipline; distinct from the `sports` interest above.
    sport
        cricket
        rowing
        rugby
        horse-racing

    # Games - the thing one plays (a hand of cards, a frame of billiards). A
    # game is a group activity OBJECT: each occasion is a per-mind game object
    # of one of these kinds (a Mental Object per knowledge_design_notes), wired
    # {@self play_game <game>} + {<game> participant <co-player>}. The
    # `(gambling)` FACET (not a kind branch) marks the money games, cross-
    # cutting the taxonomy - a card-game may or may not be played for stakes.
    # The standing DISPOSITION to gamble is the `gambling-addiction` attr
    # (common.arc), not a kind here.
    game
        card-game
            poker     (facets gambling)
            blackjack (facets gambling)
            whist
            bridge
        billiards
        dominoes      (facets gambling)

    # Occasions - a planned social gathering (a wedding, dinner party, church
    # service, market day, ...). Per the occasion/ceremony model an occasion is a
    # per-mind Mental Object (knowledge_design_notes), NOT an env entity: the host,
    # each invitee, and any onlooker each mint their OWN occasion object, all
    # anchored to the SHARED env entities (the host NPC + the venue building) plus
    # the date, so cross-mind agreement falls out of the shared anchors - there is
    # no ground-truth occasion entity, name string, or hsim-side ledger. Decorated
    # with {<occ> host <human>} / {<occ> venue <building>} / {<occ> date <date>} /
    # {<occ> hours <start> /aux <end>} (States.mon). The constitutive identity pair
    # is {host, date} (a host throws at most one thing per date). The appointment
    # beliefs that carry it are {@self organize <occ>} (host) and the told copy
    # of the host's own {<host> invite @self /aux <occ>} (guest).
    occasion
        dinner-party
        wedding
        engagement-party
        birthday-party
        sporting-occasion
        church-service
        market-day

    # Intoxicants - the abstract substance an NPC can form a `craving` for
    # (the (drive) block in States.mon) and that the drinking behaviour events
    # act on. `alcohol` is the abstract substance; the physical `beer` prop
    # (Objects.mon) is a separate, concrete layer.
    substance
        alcohol
        # Cardiac glycoside; the canonical poison in
        # the case study. Concrete bottles are `prop` entities containing it.
        digitalis

    living-arrangement  (sub human)  (tar ? @excl)
        # home-tenure: the owner-occupier arrangement (renamed from `owner` to free that
        # word from legal-ownership `own`). Target is the dwelling's owner (self or org).
        home-tenure     (tar human|org @excl)
        houseguest
        renting

    capacity            (tar ? @excl)
        pub-patron

    activity
        bartending
        
    org-pos
        apprenticeship
        membership          (sub human)
        job                 (sub human)  (disclosure stranger)
            # org-head groups every "head of an org" position, so {@self job [k org-head]}
            # matches ANY head via is-a. It is a SOCIAL marker (status / ambition's "take
            # the seat"); OPERATIONAL behaviour dispatches on duties ({@self duty-to ?org
            # [k <duty>]}), never on job kind. Head-ness is a KIND, not a rank, and a head
            # job carries NO salary (heading an org != being employed - employment = a
            # salaried job; a head who also draws a wage holds a second, staff job too).
            org-head
                # The head of a domestic household org (org household).
                head-of-household
                # The head of any non-household org (business / gov / club). Its sub-kinds
                # are the specific Victorian head titles, so a bank's banker, a museum's
                # curator etc. is-a head-of-non-household-org (the social-marker test).
                head-of-non-household-org
                    # business owner-heads (may-own in occupations.hs)
                    proprietor
                    banker
                    industrialist
                    merchant
                    solicitor
                    apothecary
                    editor
                    house-agent
                    landlord
                    # public-institution heads - one per org, distinct from their
                    # staff (priest=church, physician=hospital, principal=school,
                    # librarian=library, curator=museum, superintendent=the civic
                    # facilities: agency / registries / theatre / meeting-hall /
                    # sports-ground)
                    priest
                    physician
                    principal
                    librarian
                    curator
                    superintendent
            # --- staff / standalone occupations (NOT org heads) ---
            printer
            journalist
            clerk
            teacher
            engineer
            surgeon
            typist
            barber
            gardener
            cook
            farmer
            nurse
            # Estate manager - day-to-day authority over an estate org, but a senior
            # staff MANAGER, not the estate's owner-head.
            steward
            shop-clerk
            waiter
            maid
            bartender
            factory-worker
            # Professional race rider employed by a race-club - the ONLY
            # NPCs permitted to ride in the annual horse-racing meet
            # (hold-sporting-event). Club members attend; they never ride.
            jockey
            # University don - head + teaching staff of a university. The university head
            # is duty-assigned, so professor stays a STAFF kind (not an org-head).
            professor
            # Phase 9 senior_appointment hires public-org appointees under
            # this kind. Distinct from clerk so prestige / pretty-print can
            # render a senior official differently from an ordinary employee.
            # ("Holding a post" is just this job-state - there is no separate
            # office-as-position concept.)
            official
            # Performer parent-kind (Phase 9 dialogue) - witnesses whose job
            # is_a performer hold an audience-aware self-conception that
            # gates the theatrical register decoration.
            performer
                actor
                singer
                musician
                magician
            # The marginal stratum (serial_predation Phase 5): the socially
            # invisible class - the historical victim pool of the Cream
            # case study. NOT in the occupations table (the catalog drives
            # org-bound employment; marginal work has no org, no register,
            # no premises): assigned at immigrant spawn (spawn-immigrant,
            # k_marginal_immigrant_frac), employer-less so the labour
            # market can still hire them out of it (upward mobility), and
            # left to the existing destitute / disreputable classifiers.
            prostitute
            vagrant
            casual-laborer
                preacher
                lecturer


    # Work hours (band_deliberate substrate): a worker's shift on one weekday,
    # held on their job object as {<job> <weekday>_hours <start> <end>} - target
    # is the start hour (0..23), aux the end hour; start > end wraps past midnight
    # (a night shift). A weekday with no relation is a day off. Stamped at hire
    # from the occupation's authored shift(s) (occupations.hs).
    mon-hours           (sub human|org-pos)  (tar ? @excl)  (aux ?)
    tue-hours           (sub human|org-pos)  (tar ? @excl)  (aux ?)
    wed-hours           (sub human|org-pos)  (tar ? @excl)  (aux ?)
    thu-hours           (sub human|org-pos)  (tar ? @excl)  (aux ?)
    fri-hours           (sub human|org-pos)  (tar ? @excl)  (aux ?)
    sat-hours           (sub human|org-pos)  (tar ? @excl)  (aux ?)
    sun-hours           (sub human|org-pos)  (tar ? @excl)  (aux ?)
    # level grades a human, or a job / org-pos - the seniority WITHIN a position,
    # orthogonal to the job KIND. A trainee clerk is {@self job ?j} + {?j level trainee}.
    # (Head-ness is NOT a level; it is the job kind org-head - see the job taxonomy.)
    level               (sub human|org-pos)  (tar @excl)
            trainee
            apprentice
            junior
            regular
            senior
    # salary decorates a job object with its wage: {?j salary <amount>}. PRESENCE means
    # the job is PAID; its absence means unpaid (a head-of-household job has no salary).
    # A money-seeker gates on (not (believes {@self job.salary})). Stamped at hire from
    # the occupation's authored wage (occupations.hs); heads/unpaid roles mint no salary.
    salary              (sub org-pos)  (tar ? @excl)
    unit
        social
            family          (sub human)  (tar @excl)
    movement
        political
            suffrage
    org
        edu
            apprenticeship
            private-school
            state-school
            university
        gov
            church
            hospital
            agency
                land-registry
                company-registry
            # Public civic / cultural institutions. Founded + minimally staffed
            # at sim start by the govt-bootstrap pass (public_orgs.hsc), each
            # occupying its own building kind (businesses.hsc). They are the
            # venues the interest activity lane sends enthusiasts to (L5):
            # library <- literature/history/science, museum <- antiques,
            # meeting-hall <- suffrage + the civic default, sports-ground <-
            # sports/riding.
            library
            museum
            meeting-hall
            sports-ground
        com
            club
                # Athletic clubs - founded procedurally (k_foundable_club_kinds).
                athletic-club
                    race-club
                    rugby-union
                # Social/gentlemen's clubs - the named institutions (the Albion,
                # St-Revi, Mariner's, Meridian House, the Foundry) are specific
                # pre-placed instances, not procedurally founded.
                social-club
            business
                factory
                bank
                shipping-agent
                insurance-co
                solicitor-firm
                house-agency
                newspaper
                pawnbroker
                hotel
                restaurant
                bookseller
                grocer
                pub
                apothecary
                barbershop
                antiques-shop
                theatre
                # A property business. Covers both the landed / agricultural
                # estate and the residential-letting company a landlord runs
                # (hsim::become_landlord founds one and hires the founder as its
                # `landlord`). Owns property, generates revenue, employs people,
                # and is sold / inherited / dissolved by the ordinary org
                # lifecycle - being a landlord is therefore not a special case.
                estate
        # The staffed domestic establishment of a quality home (manor /
        # townhouse). Founded by the staff-household pass with the household
        # head as founder, seated at the home itself; employs maid / cook /
        # steward / gardener through the ordinary org machinery, so its
        # employee-register doubles as the servants' wage-book and the
        # establishment is inherited with the rest of the estate
        # (propagate_death's inherit_or_dissolve_orgs). The staff are the
        # interception / surveillance surface (see Docs/hsim/hsim_social.md).
        household

    # Fields of study were folded into the unified `domain` axis:
    # the former field_of_study leaves now live under `domain > academic-field`.
    # The `study` / `diploma` relations and `skilled-in` (States.mon) target
    # `domain` (a field-of-study is an academic-field sub-kind of domain).

    # ----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Derived situations (F3.3) - a category ("what sort of X"), each an @excl
    # noun-state classified from several dimensions by an F3.5 classifier.
    # Never authored; computed and cached. F3.6 removed the coarse social_class
    # attr: class-situation is now the sole class concept, a belief seeded by
    # mx_make_human (upper/middle/lower). Turning it into a fully derived
    # belief - the eight-value form, classified from prestige + breeding +
    # wealth - is future work and needs founder-seeded title/lineage/education
    # grounding. (`stable` / `struggling` recur across situations - a
    # deliberate scoped homonym, resolved by the field's /tar, like `medium`.)
    # ----------------------------------------------------------------------
    economic-situation       (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        destitute
        poor
        struggling
        stable
        comfortable
        prosperous
        wealthy
    # repute - PUBLIC respectability, banded per (observer, subject) by repute.hs
    # from the conduct bands + devoutness + decorum + chastity the observer holds
    # of the subject. Per-observer and non-telepathic: self reads complete inputs
    # (so self-repute IS the truth), a tracked other reads only what leaked, a
    # stranger reads middling. One belief, one classifier - no separate truth label.
    repute                   (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        exemplary
        respectable
        questionable
        disreputable
        scandalous
    # conduct-level - a shared 3-level band (lax / fair / good) for the per-observer
    # conduct dimensions (honesty / diligence / generosity / sobriety), banded PER-(mind,
    # subject): {@self <dim> <level>} from @self's own dims, {?other <dim> <level>} abduced
    # from what the observer has witnessed (unknown -> fair, the benefit of the doubt).
    # repute fuses these bands (+ devoutness for piety, the decorum float, and per-observer
    # chastity) identically for self and for a tracked other - reputation is genuinely
    # per-observer, sharpening with evidence.
    conduct-level            (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        lax
        fair
        good
    # piety-band - devoutness standing, banded from the continuous piety
    # SIGNAL by the derived-signals engine (Merlin docs/
    # derived_signals_program.md; declared in definitions/signals.hs). The
    # signal accrues per worship act and leaks monthly, so the band tracks
    # LIVED devoutness: a regular churchgoer reads devout, a lapsed one
    # slides through observant to secular over ~2 years.
    piety-band               (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        devout
        observant
        secular
    # impression - perceived-CHARACTER kinds abduced from witnessed episodes
    # (abduction v2). The (impression <attr> [k impression <leaf>] <weight>)
    # rows in definitions/signals.hs map an emitting event's trait-attr gate
    # terms to these leaves; a witness then mints {actor seems <leaf>} at the
    # authored weight. Targets of the `seems` relation (States.mon), never
    # minted as a band; NOT @excl there - the leaves are independent.
    impression               (sub human)  (tar)
        hot-tempered
        callous
        cruel
        selfish
    class-situation          (sub human)  (tar @excl)  (disclosure stranger)
        upper
        middle
        lower
    health-situation         (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        robust
        frail
        ailing
        invalid
    social-trajectory        (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        rising
        stable
        declining
    life-satisfaction        (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        fulfilled
        content
        secure-but-hollow
        struggling
        loner
        adrift

    # Perceptible life-stage. age-band is the single current band (one per
    # person, @excl - re-minted on a band crossing); a PERCEIVED approximation
    # (you can see roughly how old someone is) minted at acquaintance contact.
    # Exact age (birth-date) is communicated only to friends-and-closer. The
    # ladder is contiguous + ORDERED, deliberately NARROW under 30 and WIDE at
    # 30+, so a "same / adjacent band" peer test stands in for the old numeric
    # age-diff windows (tight among the young, loose among adults). The band
    # BOUNDARIES are the single source of truth in C++ (age_band_for); keep this
    # list in lockstep with it.
    # Bands (ranges, in lockstep with age_band_index in hsim_belief_propagation.cc):
    #   infant 0-2  juvenile 3-9  adolescent 10-15  youth 16-17
    #   young-adult 18-29  middle-aged 30-49  mature 50-69  elderly 70+
    # (`juvenile` not `child` - `child` is already the kinship bond kind.)
    age-band                 (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        infant
        juvenile
        adolescent
        youth
        young-adult
        middle-aged
        mature
        elderly
    # The proximity window: each person's own band PLUS its immediate neighbours
    # (band +/- 1), so 2-3 values. Non-@excl. Proximity ("are we age peers")
    # binds @self's single age-band and tests whether the candidate's age-span
    # covers it - i.e. |band(self) - band(other)| <= 1 (same or adjacent).
    age-span                 (sub human)  (tar age-band)

    # Derived archetypes (F3.4) - a named conjunction over situations and
    # dimensions; non-@excl, an NPC may match several. Prototype kinds are
    # added with their classifiers - these four are F3.7 / Phase 7 consumers.
    prototype                (sub human)
        deserving-poor
        undeserving-poor
        self-made-man
        nouveau-riche
        drunkard
        # fallen-woman: a woman whose sexual misconduct became PUBLICLY
        # known - the divorce that answered a discovered affair (hse_engine
        # run_generative_betrayal marks directly) or an adulterous liaison
        # at least one third mind learned of (hsim_derive
        # classify_fallen_woman, annual). Class-modulated consumers:
        # betrothal excludes her absolutely, love_match re-admits only a
        # lower-class pair (working-class pragmatism), respectable service
        # (households / schools) turns her out; the gossiped divorce
        # record's repudiation-act reactions carry the parish scorn. NOT
        # irreversible: a fall lived down quietly for a decade may
        # rehabilitate on a small annual roll.
        fallen-woman
        # for-hire: available to be hired as a contract killer (the
        # contract-killing redesign, classify_hirelings, annual). Derived
        # when the person is LETHALLY CAPABLE (skilled-in a martial leaf,
        # or illicit garrotting, or raw strength + the street-default
        # methods) AND either a BAD SEED (low compassion x high
        # disinhibition - the remorseless mercenary, reliable, repeat
        # business) OR ECONOMICALLY DESPERATE (destitute/poor - the
        # reluctant man who takes one job out of need, mints guilt, often
        # botches and never repeats). The TYPE (street tough / prizefighter
        # / discharged or serving soldier) is read from the held skills +
        # `served` belief, not a separate label. A self-belief the person
        # holds; the connection gate reads it on the instigator's
        # acquaintances.
        for-hire
        # go-between: the underworld FIXER - acquainted both upward (toward
        # respectable society) and downward (into the for-hire pool). The
        # corrupt publican / fence / flash sporting-man. Derived by
        # classify_fixers (annual). An upper-class instigator can only reach
        # a killer THROUGH one of these; takes a cut of the fee.
        go-between

    message
        declaration
        property-description
        article
        advert
        chapter
    payment
        wage
        annual-wage

    # Reified act-categories - the context-free "what kind of act" tags
    # that the appraisal pipeline reads off any anchor belief
    # (Docs/emotion/emotion_system.md).
    # FLAT vocabulary: no hierarchy among the categories - every leaf state
    # / action enumerates which categories it falls under via a
    # (construed-act tag1 tag2 ...) sexpr at declaration time. is_a checks
    # against the construed-act ROOT recognize any of these as appraisal
    # categories; specific dispatch is by direct kind comparison. The set
    # mixes (a) "what was done" categories (wrong, help, honour, intimacy,
    # ...), (b) outcome categories (suffer_loss, achieve), and (c) the
    # cross-cutting umbrellas (wrong over harm/slight/appropriation/...,
    # help over aid/provision, ...) - all flat siblings rather than nested.
    # Wronging branch  : wrong-act (umbrella) over harm/slight/appropriation/
    #                    coercion/abandonment/betray/expose/threaten - all of
    #                    them are flavors of "bad things to someone".
    # Helping branch   : help-act (umbrella) over aid (direct assistance) and
    #                    provision (giving alms / gifts / drink).
    # Honour branch    : honour-act (public recognition) plus commitment-act
    #                    (keeping a promise IS honouring).
    # Intimacy         : intimacy-act on its own. Betray-by-diversion mints a
    #                    separate betray-act construal in observer minds via
    #                    categorize()'s structural test.
    # Outcomes         : suffer-loss-act (patient lost something) and
    #                    achieve-act (actor succeeded) - outcome-based,
    #                    minted directly by hsim events when relevant.
    # neutral-act      : legacy "do not appraise" tag - kept so .act files
    #                    declaring `nature = neutral-act` keep parsing.
    #                    New code: just omit (construed-act ...) entirely.
    construed-act       (+ sub human)
        wrong-act
        harm-act
        slight-act
        appropriation-act
        coercion-act
        abandonment-act
        betray-act
        expose-act
        threaten-act
        help-act
        aid-act
        provision-act
        honour-act
        commitment-act
        intimacy-act
        suffer-loss-act
        achieve-act
        neutral-act
        # rivalrous-act: actor competes with patient for a shared scarce
        # resource (post, partner, inheritance). Distinct from slight-act
        # (which is unprovoked affront) - rivalry is positional. Mints
        # rivalry-pressure on the outcompeted patient via the reaction
        # row in appraisal.hsc. Placed at end to keep older taxonomy
        # kind ids stable.
        rivalrous-act
        # repudiation-act: actor formally casts the patient off (a husband
        # divorcing an adulterous wife). The patient bears the public
        # disgrace - shame + status-loss on the patient, third-party
        # contempt at the PATIENT (society sides with the wronged
        # husband), unlike abandonment-act where third parties fault the
        # deserter. Appended at end to keep kind ids stable.
        repudiation-act
        # degrade-act: a deliberated PUBLIC put-down - humiliation with an
        # audience. Distinct from slight-act (the dyadic insult sting):
        # the audience makes the injury a STATUS event, so the patient
        # feels shame + status-loss (the expose-act-shaped cascade)
        # without any secret being disclosed. Carried by the
        # public-humiliation perpetration leaf. Appended at end to keep
        # kind ids stable.
        degrade-act

    # Message classes - the verbal-method vocabulary, a property of the MESSAGE not
    # a task. A verbal act's memory is a SAY belief whose msg carries a (msg-class
    # <leaf>) arg; is_msg_class_label routes it to that SAY-memory form and categorize()
    # reads the leaf's (construed-act ...) off the msg-class. These are NOT tasks.
    # (+ noun): the construed-act decorations are relation flags; without the
    # explicit noun mark they would trip define()'s noun-vs-relation inference
    # (same convention as the kinship block).
    msg-class           (+ noun)
        insult          (construed-act slight-act)
        jilt            (construed-act abandonment-act wrong-act)
        urge            (construed-act coercion-act)


    sky-condition
        clear
        overcast
        cloudy

    strength-measurement
        none
        light
        medium
        heavy

    mass-measurement
        weight
    
    # Sexual orientation - a kind-typed /feel attr (common.arc). Genetic;
    # learned of others only by a spouse / immediate family (believe_about
    # Band 4). The Big Five personality aspects and the dark tetrad are 0..1
    # float attrs, not kinds, so they need no taxonomy here.
    sexual-orient           (tar @excl)
        hetero
        bi
        homo

    cultural-aspect
        title
        nationality         (sub human)  (tar @excl)  (disclosure stranger)
            english
            irish
            st-revieran
            french

    physical-quality
        color               (tar @excl)
            blue
            brown
            green
            grey
            hazel
            black
            red
            auburn
            blonde
            white
        gender              (tar @excl)  (disclosure stranger)
            male
            female
        appearance          (tar @excl)
            ugly
            plain-looking
            beautiful
        girth               (tar @excl)
            thin
            medium
            fat
        height              (tar @excl)
            short
            medium
            tall
        # Hair / eye colour (serial_predation generalized fixation): their
        # OWN leaf taxonomies (not the shared `color` palette above) so the
        # trait loader's scoped value resolution ("hair-color blonde") works
        # and a fixation value's parent kind unambiguously names its axis.
        # Repeated leaves across the two (brown / grey) are fine - scoped
        # resolution keeps them distinct, exactly like girth / height
        # `medium`. Seeded at human creation from the .txt trait tables.
        hair-color          (tar @excl)
            black
            brown
            auburn
            red
            blonde
            grey
            white
        eye-color           (tar @excl)
            blue
            brown
            green
            grey
            hazel

    blood-type          (obs) (tar @excl)
        A
        B
        AB
        O

    # game-role distinguishes the player-vs-NPC dispatch the engine
    # reads from the social-identity beliefs (the `role` identity
    # taxonomy above: parent / spouse / worker / christian / ...) that
    # the appraisal pipeline reads.
    game-role           (tar @excl)
        player
        nonplayer

    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Relational states. A noun is automatically a state, so each is
    # declared once here; States.mon holds only non-noun verb states.
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------

    # Transaction states.
    price               (tar @excl)
    item                (obs) (tar object)
    view                (obs) (sub human)  (tar @excl object)

    # Kinship and social bonds - subject and target are both human. //noun
    # makes every role explicitly a noun, so the bond decorations below
    # (relation flags) do not trip define()'s noun-vs-relation inference.
    relationship        (+ sub human)  (+ tar human)  (+ noun)
        parent          (inclusive_bond)  (close_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        mother          (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)  (close_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        father          (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)  (close_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        brother         (inclusive_bond)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        sister          (inclusive_bond)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        sibling         (inclusive_bond)  (close_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        half-sibling    (inclusive_bond)  (close_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        grandmother     (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        grandfather     (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        grandparent     (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        grandchild      (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        aunt            (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        uncle           (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        niece           (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        nephew          (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        cousin          (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        mother-in-law   (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)
        father-in-law   (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)
        parent-in-law   (inclusive_bond)
        sister-in-law   (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)
        brother-in-law  (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)
        sibling-in-law  (inclusive_bond)
        daughter-in-law (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)
        son-in-law      (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)
        child-in-law    (inclusive_bond)
        stepmother      (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)
        stepfather      (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)
        stepchild       (inclusive_bond)
        child           (inclusive_bond)  (close_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        # Guardianship. {?guardian ward ?ward_npc} reads
        # "guardian is the legal guardian of ward". Inclusive bond
        # (multiple wards possible). The case study's Ashcombe/Clara pair
        # uses this for the pre-perpetration relationship.
        ward            (inclusive_bond)  (extended_kin)
        spouse          (tar @excl)  (exclusive_bond)  (close_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        fiancee         (tar @excl)  (exclusive_bond)  (close_kin)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        lover           (inclusive_bond)  (close_kin)  (construed-act intimacy-act)  (disclosure intimate)
        friend          (inclusive_bond)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        acquaintance    (inclusive_bond)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        neighbour       (inclusive_bond)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        enemy           (inclusive_bond)
        # talk-to: on-speaking-terms social contact (appears in the relationship
        # ground-alt alongside friend/acquaintance). A human-human bond.
        talk-to         (inclusive_bond)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        # The per-mind handle for "whoever killed X": {?dead killer ?o},
        # where ?o is each mind's own imagined unknown-culprit object
        # (mx_imagine_or_recall - per-mind identity by design) until
        # evidence ever names a real person. Minted into the dead's circle
        # by the burial-verdict pass when the corpse carries violent
        # evidence (serial_predation Phase 1).
        killer
        love                    (tar ?)  (exclusive_bond)
        # Directed competitive bond. May be
        # asymmetric (A fixates on B; B indifferent). Sourced by
        # rivalry-pressure-driving events (lost-job-to, outbid-by,
        # out-courted-by). Read by deliberation affinity rows and by
        # appraisal to weight slight-act reactions higher when the
        # source is a held rival.
        rival                   (inclusive_bond)
        # Conspiracy bond. Subject = principal
        # (recruiter), target = helper. Aux carries the embedded
        # goal-fact that `recruit` minted into the helper's mind.
        # Closes the loop on the existing `recruit (tar human) (aux ?)`
        # behaviour label - recruit is the ACT, accomplice is the
        # ongoing BOND.
        accomplice              (aux ?)
        # Co-equity bond in a venture. Symmetric -
        # minted on both sides when the partnership is formed. Aux
        # carries the org. Distinct from `founder` (one-shot
        # constitutive, @excl) and `employer` (subordinate relation).
        # Same org may have many partners.
        business-partner        (aux org)

    marriage-desirability   (tar ? @excl)

    birthplace          (sub human)  (tar structure @excl)  (disclosure acquaintance)

    # Residential / venue knowledge and the apprenticeship bond (subject is a
    # human). The verb-shaped vocational relations (retire / carrying-loot /
    # since / duty-to / duty-holder / study / schooling) live in States.mon.
    vocational-state    (+ sub human)
        home                (tar structure @excl)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        # WHERE the NPC believes provisions are sold - the shop they buy food
        # at. Per-mind venue knowledge, learned honestly (the public register
        # read at orientation, or having found food at a shop's counter);
        # meals.hs provisioning / starving lanes route on it. @excl: one
        # habitual shop; a new discovery supersedes.
        provisions-shop     (tar structure @excl)  (disclosure acquaintance)
        # A private hiding-spot cache the NPC MADE (an interior sub-space they own).
        # A DEFINED relation so {@self hiding-spot <cache>} mints reasoned (/rsn) and
        # PERSISTS - an undefined label mints /obs and self-perception disproves it
        # every cycle, which re-opens the make_secret_cache gate and floods a bedroom's
        # sub-spaces. Shares its NAME with the `hiding-spot` KIND; kind references
        # disambiguate with the full path `[k interior-space hiding-spot]` /
        # mx_resolve_kind_id("interior-space hiding-spot"). Inclusive.
        hiding-spot         (tar interior-space)
        # Work life-cycle. The position is the job OBJECT ({@self job ?j}); its org,
        # wage, seniority and start-date are decorations ON that object ({?j org ?},
        # {?j salary ?}, {?j level ?}, {?j since <year>}) - there is no separate `employer`
        # relation. master is the person a youth apprentices under - a mentorship bond
        # held on the apprentice ({@self master <person>}), not a job-object decoration.
        master              (sub human)  (noun) (tar human @excl)

    # Property holdings: a holder's owned buildings and land are recorded as
    # repeated singular {holder owns-building <building>} / {holder land <land>}
    # beliefs. `land` (Spaces.mon) is a noun and so is already a state; owned
    # buildings need an explicit relation because the `building` label is reserved
    # for whereabouts ({X building <bldg>} = X is located in the building, for any
    # subject) - so ownership is a distinct `owns-building` label declared here.
    owns-building       (sub human|org)  (tar building)

    # States describing an organisation (subject is the org mental object).
    # employee is repeated once per worker; record points at the org's
    # articles-of-incorporation document.
    org-state           (+ sub org)
        informal-name       (tar ? @excl)
        founder             (tar human @excl)
        head-job            (tar org-pos @excl)
        workplace           (tar space|structure @excl)
        employee            (tar human)
        # display-ad - the org is DISPLAYING an advert for this post. An ongoing org
        # state: minted by the post-ad task when the notice goes up, ended by remove-ad
        # when it comes down. It answers "what stands", so it must never be re-derived
        # from /caused_by - that asks whether THIS task instance posted it, which
        # re-posts yesterday's opening and cannot span a shift. It is ALSO the sentence
        # the notice carries, so a seeker who READs the board adopts the same fact the
        # org holds - one term, no separate advert vocabulary.
        display-ad          (tar job)
        record              (tar document @excl)

    # Building -> tenant link: the queryable form of a lease, whose contract
    # records are the private lease-agreement documents kept at both parties'
    # premises. @excl - one ongoing tenant at a time (a re-lease opens a fresh
    # interval after the prior one ends).
    tenant              (sub building|space)  (tar human|org @excl)

    # Building -> occupant link: everyone habitually present in the building,
    # regardless of legal title - household members and staff at a home,
    # employees at a workplace. Distinct from owner / tenant (which are about
    # title); non-@excl, since a building has many occupants and a person
    # occupies both their home and their workplace.
    occupant            (sub building|space)  (tar human)

    # States describing an activity-object.
    activity-state
        participant         (tar human)
        todo                (tar task)
